From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:00:59 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 178/178] Meridian: an agent's permission question as a card
 over any page

Claude Code sessions started from the Workbench get a PermissionRequest hook
(Meridian --secret-guard --permission) that hands the question to Meridian
over the guard's socket. Mission Control keeps it (snapshot "asks") and every
window shows a small card: which session, in which space, wants what; Allow,
Deny, Always allow (Claude Code's own suggestion) and Open (its terminal, in
its space). The terminal asks too: whichever answers first counts, and the
card goes away when the session stops waiting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
